            <p>Pulmonary Vein Variants on Multiplanar Computed Tomography Reconstruction. Multiplanar volume-rendered reconstructions of the pulmonary veins and left atrium demonstrate individual anatomical variation in ostial number, caliber, course, and branching. Images were acquired using a maximum intensity projection algorithm along oblique coronal planes. Color-coded arrows mark the early branching of the lower right pulmonary vein. Contributed by Bruno Bordoni PhD</p>
